Livepaper includes code adapted from Phosphene
  https://github.com/kageroumado/phosphene  (commit 8b5bd57, 2026-09-03)

Each file below carries a header naming Phosphene.

Packages/LivepaperKit/Sources/WallpaperAgentBridgeObjC/include/WallpaperAgentBridgeObjC.h
    the private protocol and CAContext declarations
Packages/LivepaperKit/Sources/WallpaperAgentBridge/
    WallpaperAgentBridge.swift    the framework, the payload class names and the
                                  video layer's _setDisallowsVideoLayerDisplayCompositing:
    Replies.swift                 remote-context and snapshot object construction
    SettingsViewModels.swift      the Codable shims for the settings view models and
                                  the archive/unarchive class remap
    WallpaperAgentListener.swift  the NSXPCInterface per-selector class whitelist
    AgentPayload.swift            request field extraction by Mirror
    AgentConnection.swift         the acquire flow and the answers to unused calls
    RemoteContext.swift           the remote CAContext per surface
Packages/LivepaperKit/Sources/LivepaperPlayback/
    LoopEngine.swift, LoopEngine+Lifecycle.swift, LoopEngine+Feeding.swift,
    LoopEngine+Reading.swift, PassLedger.swift
                                  the two-reader gapless loop with a timestamp offset
                                  and compressed samples passed through
    SurfaceLayers.swift, SurfaceLayers+Transitions.swift, SurfaceTree.swift
                                  one layer tree per surface, built before the first
                                  reply, with both video layers made up front
    SurfaceStore.swift            surfaces that outlive the agent's connection, and
                                  the grace period before a teardown
WallpaperExtension/
    AgentRequests.swift           the acquire flow: the tree set in the context and
                                  flushed before the reply
    HostedSurfaces.swift          one remote context per surface, kept by surface ID
                                  so that it outlives the agent's connection

No GPL project was read for this work.

